## Advisories

- Fixture harness gap (most important). The plan says the fixture runs `bundle exec jekyll build` in a throwaway directory and does not load the rest of `_plugins/`. A tempdir has no Gemfile, so `bundle exec` needs `BUNDLE_GEMFILE` pointing at the repo `Gemfile`. Once that is set, `Jekyll::PluginManager.require_from_bundler` (`gemfile_exists?` checks `ENV["BUNDLE_GEMFILE"]`) runs `Bundler.require(:jekyll_plugins)` and loads every gem in the Gemfile's `jekyll_plugins` group (remote-theme, auto-authors, auto-thumbnails, mermaid-prebuild, llm-sidecars, archives, paginate-v2, seo-tag, sitemap, jektex...) into each fixture build. That slows eight builds and risks cross-gem side effects. Recommended in build: set `BUNDLE_GEMFILE` to the repo Gemfile and `JEKYLL_NO_BUNDLER_REQUIRE=1`, and give the fixture `_config.yaml` `plugins: [jekyll-feed]` (the plugin file also requires it). The fixture config also needs `collections: garden: output: true` so garden docs get URLs.
- Local environment. `bundle exec` fails here: `jekyll-remote-theme-0.6.2`, `addressable-2.9.1`, `csv-3.3.7`, `sass-embedded-1.107.1`, `listen-3.10.1` are not installed. Run `bundle install` before the red step. The full-site `bundle exec jekyll build` in the green step also depends on the remote theme fetch (`00_remote_theme_auth.rb`).
- Vacuous reds. Unpublished, empty-garden, no-garden-collection, and draft cases pass before the plugin exists (the draft case passes because the garden page is simply absent). They are regression guards, which the plan already states. Red-step expectation (dated-garden, limit, garden-alone, posts-feed-only fail) is accurate.
- Garden entries have no `author` and `_config.yaml` has no site `author`, so garden entries in the feed render `<author><name></name></author>` (posts set `author: niko`). Not in the requirements and not tested. Consider a `defaults` scope for `type: garden` setting `author`, or a fixture assertion, as a follow-up.
- Doc follow-up at reflect/archive time: `memory-bank/techContext.md` "Testing Process" describes the unittest suite as the SVG stripper only; it will also cover the feed fixture and need `bundle install` first.

## Radical innovation (advisory)

Replace the hard-coded `site.garden` with a config-driven list, e.g. `feed.also_include: [garden]` in `_config.yaml`. In `feed_template`, read `site.config["feed"]["also_include"]` (Array) and, for `page.collection == "posts"`, emit one `{% assign posts = posts | concat: site.<name> %}` per entry after the posts assign, skipping names missing from `site.collections`. This makes the plugin a generic "posts feed also lists collection X" patch, removes the per-site `garden` literal, makes the no-garden-collection guard uniform, and keeps the plan's tests intact (the fixture config just sets `feed.also_include: [garden]`). Cost: one config key and one extra fixture case (an unknown collection name is ignored).
